{"duration_api_ms":1748022,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"037cc0b5-4843-4f7e-841e-45cc8fa8c4b9","total_cost_usd":35.2744155,"usage":{"input_tokens":436,"cache_creation_input_tokens":385816,"cache_read_input_tokens":55995051,"output_tokens":136571,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":61857},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":385816,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1671,"cache_read_input_tokens":394092,"cache_creation_input_tokens":376,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":376},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":2160,"outputTokens":23,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.002275,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":436,"outputTokens":136571,"cacheReadInputTokens":55995051,"cacheCreationInputTokens":385816,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":35.2721405,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":232,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"W385424 is implemented. No `handoff/request.json` was written — nothing blocked.\n\n## What changed and why\n\nThe manager already held everything needed to explain the pilot ending; nothing composed it. The correction adds a **worker-declared axis** to the existing attempt diagnostic and teaches the two operator surfaces to read it.\n\n**Product (3 files)**\n\n- `v12/python/src/baton_v12/worker_manager/failure_cause.py` — new `worker_declaration` axis on the composed document, plus `declaration_of` beside `answer_of`/`absent_of`. The sealed half (`disposition`, `result_id`, `frozen_at`) comes off this manager's own `outputs` row; the typed half (`declared_ending`, `failure_reason`, `seconds_bound`, `seconds_bound_source`, `verification_attempted`, `verification_status`) comes from the worker's `result.json` **inside** the frozen candidate tree, read only against the byte count and content digest the manager measured when it sealed it, an artifact identity that names this exact attempt, and the indexed artifact row agreeing with the retained manifest. Every member is a closed-vocabulary word, a bounded identity, a ranged integer or a boolean.\n- `v12/python/tools/job_observation.py` — `_reason` replaces `cause unknown` (and only that) with the declaration; exchange faults and role-adapter codes keep their place ahead of it. Only a sealed `unable` speaks; `cancelled`/`completed`/`plan-rejected` render exactly as before. No new imports (the no-I/O case still holds).\n- `v12/python/tools/attempt_diagnostics.py` — the axis as its own row member under the positive allowlist, with closed-value checks on the four vocabulary members.\n- `v12/python/src/baton_v12/job_manager/projection.py` — comment only; the projection already carries the document whole and must keep deciding state from `_DISPOSITIONS` alone.\n\n**Lines deliberately not crossed:** the declaration is never folded into `cause`; `ANSWERS` is still four; `unknown`, `absent_records`, revocation and cancellation are unchanged beside it; the prose `recap` is never parsed; no path, locator or provider text is emitted; the filesystem read sits outside every transaction (DB-1/DB-4), and repeated reads write nothing.\n\n**Two judgement calls, stated rather than hidden.** (1) I did **not** bump `baton.v12.attempt-failure-cause/1`. The member is additive and every reader is a positive allowlist; a bump would make already-installed `attempt-diagnostics` bundles report *every* axis as unavailable — a larger loss than the gap. The reasoning is written into the code. (2) `declaration_of` is public, so `tests/manager/test_boundary_inventory.py` needed an owner entry (added, mirroring `absent_of`).\n\nDocs: `v12/python/JOB-VIEWER.md` gains a section on the failed-stage reason and the three rules.\n\n## Verification\n\nMandatory argv: **268 tests, OK** (was 223). Per module: `test_attempt_failure_cause` 93→113, `test_attempt_diagnostics` 42→51, `test_job_observation` 7→18, `test_job_viewer` 81→86 (+45). Also run green: `test_boundary_inventory` (380), `test_attempts`/`test_sealing`/`integration.test_driver` (611), `test_diagnostic_rendering`/`test_output`/`test_dependencies`/`test_contracts_inventory`/`test_delegation`/`test_stack` (281, 1 pre-existing skip), `job_manager.test_status`/`test_store_readonly`/`test_worker_visibility` (174), `test_sweep` (48), native-handoff/review-driver modules (259). No Docker, engine or provider calls.\n\n**Honest limitation — the mandatory command fails in *this* sandbox for an environment reason, not a code one.** Under the sandbox's `umask 0077`, `tests.tools.test_job_viewer` fails two tests (`TheRealObservationReaderReachesTheView`): the integration target is created `0o700`, the deployment denies it (\"an integration runtime holds that group as its only share in the target\"), the attempt's launch root is left behind, and the stage never leaves `claimed`. Both fail identically on the **unmodified** tree at `HEAD` and at `3d05430f`, and both pass with my changes under `umask 002` — which is how every count above was taken. Nothing else in the suite was skipped.\n\n**Other limitations:** the typed members require local custody to still hold the frozen tree; a discarded tree leaves them `unknown` with the sealed disposition still answering. The ending/failure-reason/bound-source vocabularies are mirrored from the worker image and held by an AST-read drift case rather than an import (the image carries no `baton_v12`). The deployed bundle must be rebuilt before an installed instance shows any of this.","ttft_ms":848,"type":"result","duration_ms":2325582,"uuid":"36d932a9-d300-46fd-b168-21dac2a01972","ttft_stream_ms":592,"time_to_request_ms":72,"queued_turn_count":0}
